+- **R19**: the `clear-resource` / `clear-mutation` discrepancy is withdrawn. Only an internal `re-frame.core-resources` wrapper exists; `re-frame.core` exposes `rf/clear :resource id`, and `spec/API.md` says exactly that (rf2-kuky.80). The API pages agree with each other; the earlier reading conflated an internal wrapper with a public name. The row stays MATCH. Two further agent-reported wording defects were withdrawn in the same pass because neither string exists in the tree: `:rf.resource.internal/aborted` is not on `docs/api/re-frame.resources.md` (positive control: `:rf.http/aborted` on the http page reads 4 hits) and the tutorial spells `:sensitive [[:auth :token]]`, not `:sensitive?` (`03-auth-and-forms.md:373`).
+- **R10**: split. The data-dependent read is DIVERGENT with the data waterfall marked TARGET (016 line 1307), where it had been folded into a MATCH.
+- **R15**: the DOCS cell gains the tutorial's global-scoped viewer-relative reads (a taught leak) and the fail-open write default with its dev tripwire.
+- **R5**, **R4**: ergonomics and docs cells gain the scope-mismatch tripwire and Conduit's explicit stale/GC policy. No status changed.
